# Serene Pub - Configuration
#
# Copy this file to ".env" IN YOUR DATA DIRECTORY — the folder that holds the
# database, not this one:
#     Linux    ~/.local/share/SerenePub/.env
#     Windows  %APPDATA%/SerenePub/.env
#     macOS    ~/Library/Application Support/SerenePub/.env
# (or <SERENE_PUB_DATA_DIR>/.env if you set that below).
#
# Why not here, next to the program? Because updating Serene Pub replaces this
# folder wholesale — the updater swaps it, and "extract the new zip over your
# old folder" is the manual upgrade path — so a .env kept here is deleted on
# upgrade, taking your settings with it. Some install formats can't even be
# written to (a macOS app bundle is code-signed; an AppImage is read-only).
# Your data directory is never touched by an update.
#
# A ".env" in this folder is still read, so an existing setup keeps working;
# Serene Pub names it at startup as a deprecated location. The one exception is
# SERENE_PUB_DATA_DIR below: it chooses the data directory, so it can only be
# set here or as a real environment variable.
#
# Real environment variables (a launcher script, systemd, Docker) always win
# over both files. Serene Pub prints the files it actually read at startup.
#
# Every setting below is optional — Serene Pub runs with none of them set.
# For the full reference see the in-app Documentation panel (Environment
# Variables), or docs/environment-variables.md and docs/hosting.md in the
# repository.

# ===========================================
# APPLICATION DATA DIRECTORY
# ===========================================
# Where your database, characters, chats and downloaded models are kept.
# Default: an OS-appropriate location
#   Linux    ~/.local/share/SerenePub
#   Windows  %APPDATA%/SerenePub
#   macOS    ~/Library/Application Support/SerenePub
#
# Set this to keep everything in one folder you control — a USB drive, a
# synced folder, or somewhere you back up as a unit. A relative path resolves
# against the folder you launch Serene Pub from.
#
# This is the ONE setting that has to be set here (or as a real environment
# variable) rather than in <data dir>/.env, since it is what chooses that
# directory. Keep a copy of the line somewhere outside this folder — an update
# replaces this folder and deletes it.
# SERENE_PUB_DATA_DIR=./data

# ===========================================
# SERVER CONFIGURATION
# ===========================================
# HTTP server port (the web UI)
# Default: 3000
# PORT=3000

# Which network interface the server binds to.
# Default: 0.0.0.0 (reachable from other devices on your network)
# Set to 127.0.0.1 to allow local connections only.
# HOST=0.0.0.0

# Disable automatically opening a browser tab on startup.
# Set to 1 to disable.
# SERENE_AUTO_OPEN=1

# ===========================================
# HOSTING BEHIND A REVERSE PROXY OR TUNNEL
# ===========================================
# Only relevant if you're putting nginx, Caddy, Cloudflare Tunnel or similar
# in front of Serene Pub. These two are all such a setup normally needs.
#
# One port serves the web UI and the real-time connection together, so your
# proxy only has to route PORT — but it MUST forward WebSocket upgrade
# requests (the `Upgrade` and `Connection` headers), or the page will load
# while real-time updates silently fail.

# The address your users actually type, as a full origin including the
# scheme. HTTPS detection, cookie security, and the real-time connection URL
# are all derived from it. Applied per request and matched on hostname, so
# direct access at http://localhost:3000 keeps working at the same time.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://serene.example.com

# Which addresses your proxy connects from. Accepts CIDRs, bare addresses,
# and the keywords `private` (the default), `none` and `*`. Setting this is
# what makes login rate limiting count real users rather than lumping
# everyone behind the proxy into a single bucket.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1

# ===========================================
# SESSIONS
# ===========================================
# How long a login session lasts before it expires.
# Default: 168 (7 days)
# USER_TOKEN_EXPIRATION_HOURS=168

# ===========================================
# ACCESSIBILITY
# ===========================================
# Make Document View — the simplified, high-contrast, keyboard- and
# screen-reader-friendly interface (Ctrl+Shift+Y) — the default for anyone
# who hasn't visited before. Once someone toggles it themselves, their own
# choice always wins.
# PUBLIC_DOCUMENT_VIEW_DEFAULT=true
